<h1>Tester Hub — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 26, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Tester Hub (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.testerhub</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Tester Hub is <strong>free with ads</strong> (Google AdMob). The app itself sends <strong>only what you type into its forms</strong> — your name + Gmail when you join or leave the tester pool, and app details if you are a developer adding an app. Your testing checklist is stored <strong>only on your device</strong> and never leaves your phone. We run no analytics of our own and sell no data.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>The app lists apps that are open for testing, with opt-in links. Tapping a link hands that app's real Google Play link to your <strong>system browser</strong>, outside this app — Tester Hub never touches your Google account, and your actual testing sign-up happens on Google Play, under Google's own privacy policy.</li>
  <li>When you join the pool, leave the pool, or add an app, the app sends exactly what you typed in that form to the Tester Hub service (<code>tattoo-art-customs.onrender.com/api/testers</code>) so the pool can route your Gmail onto tester lists. Nothing else is sent.</li>
  <li>Your checklist — which apps you have marked as joined — is stored <strong>only on your device</strong>, in the app's own local storage. It never leaves your phone and is never visible to us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Internet / network state</strong> — to load the live app feed, submit the forms you fill in, and load ads.</li>
  <li><strong>Advertising ID permission</strong> (<code>com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID</code>) — used by the Google Mobile Ads SDK to serve and measure ads.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>This version shows ads served by <strong>Google AdMob</strong> (banner and occasional full-screen ads). AdMob may collect and use your device's advertising ID and ad-interaction data as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. The app also shows clearly labeled "House commercials" — our own promotional cards for our apps and affiliate partners; those are served from inside the app and involve no third-party tracking.</p>

<h2>What we store</h2>
<p>If you join the pool: your name and Gmail, on the Tester Hub service, for as long as you stay in the pool — used only to route you onto tester lists. Leave the pool in the app (or email us) and it is removed from future routing. On your device: only your checklist, erased by uninstalling.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Tester Hub is a tool for adults who test apps. It is not directed at children under 13.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

